wildos-winmode (0.3.1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Windows has all the memory it is set to while any Windows app is open.
    Unused memory went back to Wild OS every 30 seconds whatever Windows
    was doing, and Windows only grew back into it a step at a time, so
    with 8 GB set it worked like a 4 GB PC: a program asking for 5 GB
    took 94 seconds to get it. Memory now goes back only while no Windows
    app is open, and the first app to open gets all of it at once,
    including one opened from inside Windows.
  * After a change of memory in Settings, an app opening before Windows
    had restarted got none of Windows' memory back: the service asked for
    the new amount, which a running Windows can't take, and libvirt
    refused the lot. It now gives back everything Windows started with,
    and the new amount comes with the restart as before.

 -- Wild OS Developers <dev@wildos.io>  Tue, 10 Nov 2026 09:30:00 +0000

wildos-winmode (0.3.0) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Setting up Windows mode: the wizard (boards 9.1 to 9.7) and the setup
    engine in the system service, from the steps tools/winmode-proof
    proved: download and check Windows, the answer file and payload, the
    isolated network, the virtual PC, the install, activation, tuning and
    Microsoft 365. Resumable, including after a restart.

 -- Wild OS Developers <dev@wildos.io>  Sun, 08 Nov 2026 10:00:00 +0000

wildos-winmode (0.2.0) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Phase 2 of Windows mode: the system service and per-user agent, the
    lifecycle and idle policy, one RemoteApp connection with apps started
    inside it by wild-guest, Start entries and file types, theme sync, and
    wild-run with the first compatibility list.

